(1) THE COUNTING IDENTITY, DERIVED FROM SCRATCH
    n = 49, d = 24: m = 588 (the paper's 588: match)
    sum_v e(G^+_v) = 3t and sum_v e(G^-_v) = m + 3t, so the difference is exactly m = 588, independently of t
    C(24,2) = 276; sum_v [e(G^+_v) + e(comp G^-_v)] = 49 * 276 - 588 = 12936 (the paper's 12936: match)
    average per vertex = 12936 / 49 = 264 (exact: True), and 2 * 132 = 264 -> both terms forced to 132
    with E(4,5,24) = 133 instead: 2 * 133 = 266 > 264, so nothing would be forced -> the lemma fails

